\f1\i0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo stared at Johnny the way one might examine a particularly persistent mosquito. Kleoboulos muttered something in Ancient Greek that sounded like a curse, or possibly a prayer for patience. Chilo studied the fire pit embers with sudden fascination.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Gentlemen,\'94 Johnny said, as he commandeered a glass, opened the bottle, sniffed the cork, and poured without offering it to anyone else. \'93You know, the cosmos has a strange sense of humour. Here I am, surrounded by individuals of such remarkable purpose, and here we are at a barbecue. Can you imagine the parallels? The charred edges of a particularly stubborn steak and, say, the outermost frequencies of universal gravitational constants? The way heat transforms matter at a molecular level mirrors the way\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Johnny,\'94 Kleoboulos interrupted, his voice steady with the authority of having completely had enough. \'93Why are you here?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny pivoted smoothly, unruffled. \'93Sublime Point is a community, isn\'92t it? And community is built on spontaneous connection. On serendipitous convergence. On\'97\'94\
