<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny turned to her with theatrical solemnity. \'93Sarah. I was hoping you\'92d be here.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You knew I\'92d be here.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Mr Stoat\'97\'94 Padmala began.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Johnny.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Mr Stoat,\'94 she continued with perfect hostess ice, \'93it\'92s been... enlightening. But our evening is winding down.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Of course, of course,\'94 Johnny said, showing no signs of leaving. He drifted toward the fire pit, admiring his own shoes as he walked. \'93I\'92ll just warm myself by your magnificent fire for a moment. You know, fire is humanity\'92s first technology. The original disruption. When you think about it, every barbecue is a ritualistic commemoration of our species\'92 conquest of thermodynamics.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo coughed into his wine. Solo buried his face in his hands. Kleoboulos simply stared at Johnny with the kind of look that could wilt stands of sugar cane.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Within minutes, through some alchemy of persistence and obliviousness, Johnny\'92s presence softened from intrusion to nuisance to grudging tolerance. He positioned himself by the fire, holding court on topics no one had asked about, while others exchanged looks that ranged from amusement to exasperation.\
